            rlp, rmp, _ = _lint_metrics(proj)
            poison_rc.append((rlp, rmp))
        # F-0123 human ruling #2 (2026-07-28): a COMPOSITE corrupt file — a wrong header+delimiter
        # BEFORE the canonical one, a delimiter with no header, or a SECOND canonical header —
        # must fail closed too. The wide `LEDGER_HEADER_RE`/`LEDGER_SEP_RE` skip-filters in
        # `ledger_malformed_rows` hid the early junk so the file certified as a pure table; now
        # ONLY the canonical header and the delimiter DIRECTLY following it are structural, every
        # other pipe line (incl. a stray junk header and a second canonical header) is a data row
        # and, not parsing as one, is flagged malformed -> lint AND metrics fail closed. Mutation
        # guard: restore the old wide `LEDGER_HEADER_RE`/`LEDGER_SEP_RE` skip-filters in
        # `ledger_malformed_rows` and every composite case goes red (the junk header AND its
        # junk delimiter slip back through as 'structure').
        good = hdr + "|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n"                            # the one legal empty ledger
        composite_poison = [
            ("| id | title | garbage |\n|---|---|---|\n" + good),            # 3-col table before canonical
            ("| id | title | severity | status | next | updated | extra |\n"
